#reason src/main/skills-catalogue.ts Gives the window one place to list a skills repo and to find the repo of the skill linker, so both tabs read the same catalogue.
#reason test/helpers/skill-linker-repo.ts The unit test and the Electron harness both need the same fixture repo with role folders and an executable linker.
#reason test/skills-linker-repo.test.ts Fails on the old code: a linker with no saved repo must give the catalogue, links and counts, and a saved repo must still win.
#reason src/main/extensions.ts The linker status needs the skill and role counts, and must resolve SKILL_LINKER the way the catalogue does.
#reason src/main/skills.ts A linker set on its own left the window with no skills, so the repo now falls back to the linker's without writing or publishing it.
#reason src/renderer/features/skills-extras.ts Attaching a missing skill links it first so a delegate can read it, and the linker row can be reused where no linker is set.
#reason src/renderer/features/skills-roles.ts Carries the repo skills to the rows so only a linkable missing skill gets the link action.
#reason src/renderer/features/skills-rows.ts A skill that is not installed has to look different from an installed one, and an attached one needs a Link to project action.
#reason src/renderer/features/skills-state.ts Candidates must say whether a skill is installed and whether it can be linked into the open project.
#reason src/renderer/features/skills.ts The first tab asked for another tab when no linker was set, so it now holds the linker row and refreshes the catalogue after a save.
#reason src/shared/lang/en/messages.json The status said only Initialized, so every linker state now has a plain sentence, and the new link and not-installed texts live here.
#reason test/e2e/app/skills-extras-main.ts The harness needs the real link and unlink channels to exercise the new actions.
#reason test/e2e/skills-extras.spec.ts Proves in the real window that the first tab lists the linker's roles, searching web finds web-research and linking works.
#reason test/e2e/support/skills-extras-harness.ts The scenarios need a fixture skills repo and a saved or unsaved linker in the temporary home.
#reason test/extensions-panel.test.ts The empty panel now carries zero skill and role counts.
#reason test/skills-extras.test.ts Covers attach-and-link, a failed link attaching nothing, Link to project and the plain-word linker sentences.
#reason test/skills-modal-scroll.test.ts The faked panel gained the skill and role counts.
#reason test/skills-modal.test.ts Covers the linker row on the first tab, in-place fill after Save and the problem shown for a bad path.
#reason test/skills-state.test.ts Covers the installed flag of candidates and the rule for linking a skill into the project.
#reason test/skills-unconfigured.test.ts The no-repo cases must not read the developer's real home, which can now hold a linker.
#story A user sets the skill linker and gets their skills
#step actor A user with a skill linker
